    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s growth story spans from 1857 to 1975, documented in a National Register Multiple Property Documentation.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.kansashistory.gov/natreg/natreg_thematics/view/25"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Highland’s railroad arrived only in 1908, much later than neighboring Kansas towns.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.kansashistory.gov/natreg/natreg_thematics/view/25"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In 2017, Highland incorporated by merging 21 subdivisions around the Crazy Horse Golf Club to address road maintenance.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Highlands%2C_Kansas"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "That 2017 incorporation made Highland the first new city in Reno County in 65 years.",
